This component mixes several unrelated concerns in one unit: (1) data fetching via a `useEffect` with a `useLayoutEffect` + `useRef` guard to prevent re-fetch loops, (2) eligibility/visibility determination from the policy collection, (3) heavy data transformation (`getSections` + `getSortedSections`) computed in the render body on every render, and (4) conditional UI rendering across three states (offline, error, chart). The `useLayoutEffect` + ref + `useEffect` interplay is particularly non-obvious and hard to reason about in isolation.

Extract the data-fetching, loading-guard, and transformation logic into a focused custom hook (e.g., `useSpendOverTimeData`). The component then becomes a thin rendering layer:
```tsx
function useSpendOverTimeData(isVisible: boolean) {
    // Owns: search effect, loading-ref guard, getSortedSections call
    return { sortedData, isLoading, hasError, isOffline };
}
```

