This `useEffect` adds a Google Tag Manager analytics concern that is specific to a single tooltip (`SCAN_TEST_TOOLTIP_MANAGER`) into `useProductTrainingContext`, a shared hook consumed by 15+ components for all tooltip types. This mixes an unrelated responsibility (analytics tracking for one specific tooltip) into a hook whose responsibility is tooltip lifecycle management (registration, visibility, rendering). Every consumer of `useProductTrainingContext` now executes this effect and its guard condition on every render cycle, even though only one tooltip type needs it. Adding more tooltip-specific analytics in the future would further bloat this shared hook.

Move the GTM event publishing to the call site that uses `SCAN_TEST_TOOLTIP_MANAGER`, or extract it into a small focused hook (e.g., `useTrackScanTestTooltip`) that the specific consumer composes alongside `useProductTrainingContext`:

```tsx
// At the call site that uses SCAN_TEST_TOOLTIP_MANAGER:
const {shouldShowProductTrainingTooltip} = useProductTrainingContext(CONST.PRODUCT_TRAINING_TOOLTIP_NAMES.SCAN_TEST_TOOLTIP_MANAGER, shouldShow);
const {accountID} = useCurrentUserPersonalDetails();

useEffect(() => {
    if (!shouldShowProductTrainingTooltip) {
        return;
    }
    GoogleTagManager.publishEvent(CONST.ANALYTICS.EVENT.PRODUCT_TRAINING_SCAN_TEST_TOOLTIP_SHOWN, accountID);
}, [shouldShowProductTrainingTooltip, accountID]);
```

